      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Improve Kimi K2 credential errors",
        "body": "## Summary\n- trim Kimi K2 API keys before constructing the Authorization header\n- classify HTTP **401** as invalid credentials (wrong/revoked/expired key) with an actionable message\n- preserve the response body for **403** and other non-200 responses as an `apiError`, so insufficient-credit / permission failures stay actionable instead of mislabeling a valid key as invalid\n\n## Why 403 is no longer mapped to invalidCredentials\n\nKimrel's docs describe `403` as insufficient credits or missing permissions, not a credential failure. The previous iteration mapped both `401` and `403` to `invalidCredentials`, which would tell a user with a **valid** key but no credits that their key is invalid or expired, while discarding the response body that carried the real reason. Now only `401` is an auth failure; `403` (and any other non-200) keeps the body on the `apiError` path.\n\n## Production-path proof\n\nA source-blind executable linked against `CodexBarCore` exercised the public fetcher through an isolated HTTP transport:\n\n```text\nPASS success-and-trim\nPASS rejected-401\nPASS rejected-403\nPASS server-error\nRESULT PASS 4/4\n```\n\nThe freshly packaged `CodexBarCLI` also called the real legacy endpoint with a synthetic invalid key. Both output formats returned exit 1 with the exact actionable message:\n\n```text\nError: Kimi K2 API key is invalid or expired.\n```\n\nThe JSON path returned the same message as a provider error. No real secret was used for the rejection proof; the 401 path is what a wrong/revoked key hits.\n\n## Note for the maintainer\nAuthenticated success proof remains blocked: no live Kimi K2 account with credits was available, so the success path is covered by the focused injected-transport tests. No CHANGELOG entry is included (release-owned); the maintainer can credit `@joeVenner` at release time as with the merged Kimi K2 follow-ups.\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter KimiK2UsageFetcherTests` (13 passed, incl. `maps 401 to invalid credentials` and `maps 403 insufficient credits to a body preserving api error`)\n- packaged CLI real-endpoint rejection proof above (401 → `Error: Kimi K2 API key is invalid or expired.`)\n- `swift build` clean\n",
